Now, we understand url redirecting :

url redirecting status code 301/302


301 -> Permanent Redirect , browser saves url in cache

-Tells the browser: "this short URL will ALWAYS point to this long URL — remember it."
-Browsers cache this — next time the user clicks the same short link, the browser redirects them without even asking your server(url shortner server), using its cached memory.

use this when we want to reduce the server load

302 - Temporary redirect

- Browsers do NOT cache this — every single click hits your server again to ask "where do I redirect this time?"

use this to keep a track of click rate



